FOUNDATION 7—DEVELOPING IN A
FISCALLY RESPONSIBLE WAY
The Cheyenne Area excels in providing services in a
fiscally responsible way.  Citizens are generally pleased
with their current levels of services and efficiency of
government according to prior surveys.  Our residents
feel safe, have access to health care and other essential
services and utilities, and appreciate quality of life
amenities, such as parks and libraries.
This Plan aims to guide future growth to promote
efficient use of public and private resources and to
provide adequate public facilities to sustain our quality
of life and to encourage continued growth. On the
private side, new development should “pay its own
way” and provide the necessary services for the new
development concurrent with the development.
Government and the public should determine how to
invest our fiscal resources strategically to achieve the
vision and principles outlined in this Plan.
